--
-- SPE-2 CARTESIAN SINGLE-WELL DRAWDOWN (HETEROGENEOUS POROSITY)
-- Generated by ./make_decks.py -- edit that file, not this one.
--
-- Cartesian re-gridding of the Second SPE Comparative Solution Project
--   H.G. Weinstein, J.E. Chappelear, J.S. Nolen, "Second Comparative
--   Solution Project: A Three-Phase Coning Study," JPT 38(3): 345-353,
--   March 1986.  SPE-10489-PA.
-- Parent radial deck: data/spe2/SPE2.DATA
--
-- What is carried over unchanged from the parent:
--   * the 15 vertical layers and their Table-2 thickness, kx, kz (kz/kx = 0.1)
--     and reference porosity (the latter as the layer mean in the
--     heterogeneous variant),
--   * PERMY = PERMX (the parent deck's COPY behaviour),
--   * the layer 7 + 8 completion and its Table-3 kh, skin and 0.5 ft
--     wellbore diameter,
--   * all fluid data (SWOF, SGOF, PVTO, PVDG, PVTW, DENSITY, ROCK, STONE1),
--   * the contacts (GOC 9035 ft, WOC 9209 ft), the 3600 psia datum at the
--     GOC, the 9000 ft formation top and the 9110 ft BHP reference depth.
--
-- What changes:
--   * GRID.  The Table-3 radial block boundaries
--       0.25, 2.00, 4.32, 9.33, 20.17, 43.56, 94.11, 203.32, 439.24,
--       948.92, 2050.00 ft
--     are mirrored about the well axis to give x- and y-face positions at
--     the same distances on either side.  The mesh is therefore a square
--     4100 x 4100 ft cross section -- 2050 ft from the well centre to each
--     of the four edges -- discretised as 21 x 21 x 15 = 6615 blocks whose
--     plan size grows logarithmically away from the centre.  The central
--     column (I,J) = (11,11) is exactly the 0.5 ft wellbore footprint.
--   * SCHEDULE.  The four-period coning schedule is replaced by a single
--     fixed 400 STB/D oil rate held for the full 900 days, so the well
--     produces a clean, continuously declining pressure transient.  The
--     Table-3 3000 psi minimum BHFP is retained only as a safety limit.
--   * Report times are graded (logarithmic over the first day, then linear)
--     for semilog / log-log well-test diagnostics.
--   * PORO is a frozen per-cell Gaussian realisation about the Table-2
--     layer means (10% CV, floored at 0.05) instead of a layer constant.
-- =====================================================================

RUNSPEC
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------

TITLE
   SPE-2 CARTESIAN DRAWDOWN - HETEROGENEOUS POROSITY

-- Mirrored radial grading: 10 rings + well column + 10 rings in each of x
-- and y, over the 15 Table-2 layers.
DIMENS
   21 21 15 /

OIL
WATER
GAS
-- Live oil with dissolved gas (black oil); no vaporized oil in SPE-2.
DISGAS

FIELD

START
   1 'JAN' 1982 /

WELLDIMS
-- 1 well, completed in 2 layers, 1 group, 1 well/group.
   1 2 1 1 /

TABDIMS
-- 1 sat-fn region, 1 PVT region; node counts sized for Tables 4 and 5.
   1 1 20 30 1 30 /

EQLDIMS
-- 1 equilibration region; raise the depth-node count for RSVD/initialisation.
   1 100 20 1 20 /

UNIFOUT

GRID
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
INIT

-- Column widths (ft), -x edge -> +x edge.  Reversed Table-3 ring widths,
-- the 2*rw = 0.5 ft well cell, then the ring widths again; they sum to
-- 2 * 2050 = 4100 ft.
DXV
   1101.08 509.68 235.92 109.21 50.55 23.39 10.84
   5.01 2.32 1.75 0.5 1.75 2.32 5.01
   10.84 23.39 50.55 109.21 235.92 509.68 1101.08 /

-- Identical grading in y: the cross section is square about the well.
DYV
   1101.08 509.68 235.92 109.21 50.55 23.39 10.84
   5.01 2.32 1.75 0.5 1.75 2.32 5.01
   10.84 23.39 50.55 109.21 235.92 509.68 1101.08 /

-- Layer thicknesses (ft), top -> bottom, one value per layer (Table 2).
DZV
   20 15 26 15 16 14 8 8 18 12 19 18 20 50 100 /

-- Depth to top of formation = 9000 ft (Table 3), flat over the 21x21 plan.
TOPS
   441*9000 /

-- Horizontal permeability kx (md) by layer, Table 2.
PERMX
   441*35   441*47.5   441*148   441*202   441*90
   441*418.5   441*775   441*60   441*682   441*472
   441*125   441*300   441*137.5   441*191   441*350 /

-- ky = kx, carrying over the parent deck's COPY behaviour: the Table-2 Kx
-- column is the permeability in both horizontal directions.
COPY
   PERMX PERMY /
/

-- Vertical permeability kz (md) by layer, Table 2 (kz/kx = 0.1).
PERMZ
