-- Field averages and fluids in place.
FPR
FOIP
FWIP
FGIP

SCHEDULE
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Central producer in column (I,J) = (11,11); BHP reference at the Table-3
-- pump depth 9110 ft.
WELSPECS
   'PROD' 'G1' 11 11 9110 'OIL' /
/

-- Completed in layers 7 and 8 (Table 3), 0.5 ft wellbore diameter, zero skin.
-- The connection transmissibility factor (item 8) is supplied explicitly:
-- the central cell is exactly the wellbore footprint (dx = dy = 2*rw), so
-- Peaceman's equivalent radius r_o = 0.198*dx = 0.099 ft falls inside rw and
-- the geometric well index is undefined.  The parent radial values are used
-- instead, T = 2*pi*0.001127*Kh / (ln(r1/rw) + skin) with r1 = 0.8416 ft:
--   layer 7: Kh = 6200 md-ft -> T = 36.17
--   layer 8: Kh =  480 md-ft -> T = 2.80
-- so the Cartesian well reproduces the SPE-2 productivity index exactly.
COMPDAT
   'PROD' 11 11 7 7 'OPEN' 1* 36.17 0.5 1* 0 /
   'PROD' 11 11 8 8 'OPEN' 1* 2.80  0.5 1* 0 /
/

-- Numerical controls only: start from a 1e-4 day step so the logarithmic
-- early-time reports are resolved, and cap the internal step at 5 days.
TUNING
   0.0001 5.0 /
   /
   /

-- Single fixed oil rate of 1000 STB/D for the whole 900 days, with the
-- Table-3 100 psi minimum BHFP retained as a safety constraint.
WCONPROD
   'PROD' 'OPEN' 'ORAT' 1000 4* 100 /
/

-- 254 report steps: logarithmic over day 1, then 0.5 d to day 10,
-- 2 d to day 100 and 5 d to day 900.
TSTEP
